# Intentional kiss-back (coup-dur): yellow rebounds from the left rail and recontacts the cue before the score.
# Source: whitepapers/the_art_of_billiards_play.html ("Coup-dur": kiss-back when the first object ball is near/frozen to a cushion).
# Pattern reference: Robert Byrne, "Shots From A Master Play," USBA/PQB April-May 2013 newsletter.
# Goal: this variation keeps the cue off the cushion while the yellow starts near it,
# preserves the deliberate second yellow contact, then sends the cue around right/top/left to red.
table three_cushion_carom_10ft
game three_cushion
ball cue at (2.000000000, 0.200000000)
ball yellow at (1.000000000, 0.086700000)
ball red at (2.122000000, 2.862000000)
cue_strike(default).mass_ratio(1.0).energy_loss(0.08)
simulation(default)
  .preset(three_cushion)
  .max_events(60)
trace(max_events: 60)
shot(cue).heading(262.879383585deg).speed(211.685360723ips).tip(side: -0.453557688R, height: 0.086501605R).elevation(0deg).using(default)
